WEBVTT

00:04:55.541 --> 00:05:00.296
The moment that happens 
marks its exact annihilation partner.

00:05:00.296 --> 00:05:03.424
Again, our introduction of pairs 
reflects this;

00:05:03.424 --> 00:05:07.428
nestled pairs only delay the inevitable
for the outer cubes.

00:05:08.804 --> 00:05:10.931
We can now program the device.

00:05:10.931 --> 00:05:15.144
Start a running sum with +1,
representing you,

00:05:15.144 --> 00:05:17.563
and scan around the circle.

00:05:17.563 --> 00:05:19.899
For each matter cube, add one,

00:05:19.899 --> 00:05:23.152
and for each antimatter cube, 
subtract one.

00:05:23.152 --> 00:05:28.657
If all 54,364 cubes have been scanned

00:05:28.657 --> 00:05:31.577
without the sum ever hitting 0,